Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:23:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] J714s: make Finish setup's Install hard to miss

omarchy-j714s 1 left the new stub unenrolled (Not Paired, Security Mode
Full, no custom kernel collection): Omarchy's Finish setup never ran, so
the Mac could not start Omarchy (docs/install-failure-2026-11-13.md).
The handoff copy said only "Finish setup at startup"; it now names the
whole step and the wrong turn.

macOS app (OmarchyInstallerUXCore, PlainLanguage):
- nextActionMessage(.enterRecovery): "Omarchy's files are in place, but
  this Mac can't start Omarchy until you finish setup. Shut down, hold
  the power button until startup options appear, pick the highlighted
  Omarchy, sign in, then click Install in Omarchy's Finish setup. Don't
  use Startup Security Utility." (recoveryInstruction). The encryption
  warnings still follow it.
- recoverySteps step 3: "Click Install in Finish setup", detail "Pick the
  highlighted Omarchy, click Continue and sign in with your macOS
  account, then click Install in Omarchy's Finish setup. Don't use
  Startup Security Utility." (recoveryFinishSetupDetail).
- The reopened-installer handoff (OnePageInstallerView
  pendingRecoveryHandoff) step 3 says the same.
- PlainLanguageTests pin the new message and step.

Recovery app (auto-launched in the stub's Recovery):
- AuthorizationPrompt.introduction (install only): "This step lets this
  Mac start Omarchy. Click Install here to finish it. Don't use Startup
  Security Utility instead." InstallerView shows it above the password
  request on the first screen.
- EnrollmentGate: the not-in-Recovery, wrong-pair and ordinary-Recovery
  messages end at Install in Finish setup and say not to use Startup
  Security Utility.
- AuthorizationPromptCheck and EnrollmentGateCheck pin the copy.

README.md (requirements, Install step 5, What the installer does step 5)
and Recovery/README.md match.

Checked on Linux (Swift 6.2 container): AuthorizationPromptCheck and
EnrollmentGateCheck compiled and passed; swift-format 6.2.4 lint --strict
passes on every changed Swift file. Not compiled: PlainLanguage.swift and
the UXCore tests (macOS-only, #if os(macOS)), OnePageInstallerView.swift
and InstallerView.swift (AppKit/SwiftUI). They need the macOS CI run
(checks.yml macos job / installer-app.yml: swift-format, debug and release
Swift tests, Recovery build-app.sh fixtures), and a look at the Recovery
first screen at its 780x440 window with the added introduction.

The Recovery tree changes again, so build-input-provenance.json's
recovery block (patches-j714s 0007) must follow that macOS run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
